Terminal 208 -> 210: the counter blocking two Maryland packets was measuring nothing\n\nFIX160 was sent to answer requiredComponentsMissing on the last two\nBUILT_RASTER_PENDING families and found the counter was never counting\ncomponents. It is the catch-all exception sink of the MD conditional\nadapter: any throw was relabelled requiredComponentsMissing: 1, the other\neight measured counters overwritten with null, and the totals zeroed. The\npublished finding named no document at all -- it was an assert.equal\nmessage comparing a result class.\n\nThe throw underneath it was NOT_MEASURABLE_HERE on visualDefects, which\nis null because no artifact record carries the glyph-geometry reading.\nThat pass is run by the central raster gate. So the counter was refusing\nboth families from the very gate that measures the one thing they could\nnot measure.\n\nIt proved outcome rather than asserting it: auditPreparedInputs over all\n43 fixtures of both families reads requiredComponentsMissing 0 on every\none with zero component findings, while the same code path returns real\nnonzero readings on the diagnostic fixtures -- so the zero is a\nmeasurement, not a silent path. Seven guards were broken deliberately and\nall seven fired, with an unbroken control accepted first and the manifest\nrestored byte-identical.\n\nBoth families move BUILT_RASTER_PENDING -> COMPLETE_PACKET_PROVEN on\nreceipts they already held. I checked that rather than take the\ntransition: run 34257213865 binds 5456086653a6f033 and run 34257872586\nbinds f23b8e7f42643090, and I recomputed both canonical files from disk\nhere -- they match the receipt and the queue exactly. Zero bytes moved,\nso those receipts still describe these packets and no raster was skipped.\n\nFACTORY-WIDE: requiredComponentsMissing is now 0 everywhere, because every\noccurrence it has ever had was this sink. The sink also erased the\nfactory's aggregates -- counterTotals went from six nulls to real numbers.\nIt survives verbatim in ky-native-candidate.mjs and\nmd-favorable-native-candidate.mjs, which FIX160 did not own and did not\ntouch.\n\nNOT REPAIRED, and correctly so: both Maryland packets deliver MDJ-008, a\nrestricted-information notice neither packet-set manifest declares, bound\ninto every waiver fixture. FIX160 did not add it to the manifest, because\ndeclaring a component is a legal-design decision and authoring one there\nwould be fabricating it. It blocks approved_for_live and any commercial\nroute for both families; it does not block the visual gate, which\npromotes nothing.\n\nVF53 also lands here. The WV composed-treatment family is\nPASS_COMPLETE_INDEPENDENT, fifteen of fifteen, and moves to\nBUILT_RASTER_PENDING -- its receipt binds 58487688 and the bytes are\n7a4c4974, so it owes a fresh raster, which VF53 does not claim.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T15:54:54Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","full_name":"Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","private":false,"owner":{"login":"Roger-LegalEase","id":287531360,"node_id":"U_kgDOESNhYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287531360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase","html_url":"https://github.com/Roger-LegalEase","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/use